This v2 includes a bug fix, and the following issue applies to that version:
The Explosion of Tensorial Variance (Gradient Death): Yes, L.I.A.R. suffers exactly from this mathematical cancer. On lines 179 and 185 of liar_neuron.py, E_tensor and E_tri brutally sum matrix products 
without dividing by $\sqrt{d_{in}}$ or $d_{in}$. For a parity of N=8 or N=16, L.I.A.R. v2 will saturate its tanh and see its gradient die !
(Bonus not listed: L.I.A.R. also suffers from the bug where the Phase Wave is computed on the noisy x_mod instead of the pure x_log, line 193).
